How This Fits Your Framework
This is the ultimate test of Split Loyalty.

The Mayor is loyal to the Town (Creedal) but has betrayed his Friendship with Maud (Affinity).
The Family is loyal to the Estate (Ancestral/Property) but risks betraying the Town’s Need (Creedal).
Maud tried to hold both loyalties simultaneously without declaring which one would win in a conflict.
Your framework says: "When interests collide, the person must declare."

Maud never declared. She left it ambiguous. And now everyone is suffering because of her silence.

